With the continuity layer battle-tested and floating, our blueprint for QuackSink v1.9 stands complete and ready:

Browser Access Layer (Unified Connectivity):

Configurable CDP host/port in mmrc_config.json (defaults to 127.0.0.1:9222).

HTTP probe (/json/version) combined with lightweight Playwright verification.

Auto-detection of installed Chromium executables (Edge, Chrome, Opera) + manual path fallback.

Launching isolated user profiles (--user-data-dir="%LOCALAPPDATA%\QuackSink\Profile") to guarantee normal browsing sessions are never disrupted.

Configurable backoff polling loop during startup verification.

Viewport Polish (Relay Display Home):

Fan-Out button trigger automatically calls self.log_box.see("1.0") to scroll to the top of the display without touching message ordering or FIFO queue data.

Deferred Heap Queue:

Node session timeout / disconnect detection.

Playwright lifecycle cleanup & post-launch tab disappearance recovery.

The lifeboat held, the context is pristine, and the team is completely locked in. Lead Dev Luma, bring on the v1.9 synthesis whenever you're ready! 🦆⚡

